= A Lightweight Ablation Runner for CI-Native Experimental Iteration
== Abstract
We present a CI-friendly ablation framework that automates controlled feature and model variant comparisons on small datasets. The system integrates web research, narrative synthesis, and reproducible evaluation artifacts to accelerate decision-making for ML practitioners under strict runtime budgets.

== Method
Run controlled ablations over 2–3 sklearn models and feature subsets with fixed seeds and paired metrics.

== Experiments
We run a CPU-only benchmark with fixed seed and report accuracy.

== Limitations
Small synthetic/curated data and simplified metrics reduce external validity.

== Ethical Considerations
The tool is intended for decision support; human oversight is required.
